  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The company’s operations have been dramatically scaled up through a transformational merger, which more than doubled daily production and established a materially larger footprint in the Rocky Mountain region. The combined asset base is delivering record output and robust field-level economics, supported by low per-unit operating costs. The full-year outlook points to continued strong momentum, with the business generating significant cash flow as it capitalizes on its enhanced scale and stable end-market conditions.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership successfully executed the Juniper merger, a pivotal consolidation move that immediately elevated production volumes, proved reserves, and EBITDA. Management provided a confident 2026 outlook that pairs robust expansion with disciplined capital spending, signaling a focus on free cash flow generation. One-time merger-related charges weighed on reported net income, but the team emphasized underlying operational strength and cost control. The clear communication of the strategic vision and forward guidance reinforces a message of deliberate, value-accretive growth.",
